{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792313330,"nonce":"ygPrcMEvZvqoPa6GLQIuJTa3Aoc=","title":"Resizable's divider has no resize cursor, and a drag loses its cursor when the pointer leaves it","message":"The user's report: a resizable panel needs an accurate cursor when its divider is hovered and while it is dragged.\n\n**What happened**\n\n`.ui-resizable-handle` set no `cursor`, so the pointer stayed the default arrow over a divider. And the cursor was taken from the nodes under the pointer only, so even a cursor set on the handle was lost as soon as a drag ran ahead of it: at a panel's minimum or maximum the pointer is off the handle for the rest of the drag.\n\n**Fix**\n\nThe handle's cursor is `col-resize`, and `row-resize` in a vertical group. While the left button is held, the cursor follows the nodes the button went down on, as a captured pointer does, and the pointer's own nodes again on release. That applies to any element, not only the divider: a slider, a scrollbar thumb or a text drag keeps its cursor the same way.","files":null}]}